 Production systems fail in fairly predictable ways: network issues (timeouts, DNS problems), rate limiting, quota exhaustion, provider-side outages, malformed requests, and authentication failures. None of these are exotic, which is exactly why they're worth designing for deliberately rather than discovering them in production.
 
